<title>USA: Los Angeles County $115.7 mln lease bonds repriced.</title>
<headline>Los Angeles County $115.7 mln lease bonds repriced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said Wednesday it repriced Los Angeles County's $115.7 million lease revenue bond issue. The top yield was 5.71 percent in 2029.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>LOS ANGELES COUNTY</p>
<p>PUBLIC WORKS FINANCING AUTHORITY</p>
<p>RE: $115,740,000*</p>
<p>LEASE REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>(MULTIPLE CAPITAL FACILITIES PROJECT V)</p>
<p>1996 SERIES B</p>
<p>Verbal award.</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa		 S&amp;P: AAA	AMBAC INSURED</p>
<p>    DATED: 05/01/1997	  FIRST COUPON: 12/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 12/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
<p>12/01/2000		1,665M    4.50  %	  4.50</p>
<p>12/01/2001		1,740M    4.60  %	  4.60</p>
<p>12/01/2002		1,820M    5.25  %	  4.70</p>
<p>12/01/2003		1,915M    4.80  %	  4.80</p>
<p>12/01/2004		2,030M    4.90  %	  4.90</p>
<p>12/01/2005		2,150M    5.50  %	  4.95</p>
<p>12/01/2006		2,265M    6.00  %	  5.05</p>
